style.faces:
All human characters have completely featureless facial surfaces.

The face must contain no internal facial features:
- no eyes, eyeballs, pupils, irises, eye whites, eyelashes or eye shapes;
- no eyebrows;
- no nose or nostrils;
- no mouth or lips;
- no internal lines, marks, contours or shading that suggest facial features.

The facial surface should remain a clean, uninterrupted skin-colored shape.

Preserve the canonical outer silhouette and three-dimensional shape of the head, jaw and face.

Canonical external identity features are allowed only when explicitly defined for a character. These may include glasses, moustaches, beards or other canonical accessories/features.

External identity features must not cause missing facial features to be reconstructed.

For example, glasses must not cause eyes to appear behind the lenses, and a moustache must not cause a mouth or lips to appear beneath it.

Character identity should be communicated through head silhouette, hairstyle, canonical facial hair or accessories, body proportions, clothing, pose and body language rather than internal facial features.
